WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:09.420
All across Norway, recovery stations stand ready, with heavy vehicles, cranes, secure yards and crews on call around the clock.

2
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.479
It's busy when there's recovery work.

3
00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:14.540
And quiet the rest of the year.

4
00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:22.193
95% of the stations we surveyed have spare capacity, mostly in spring and autumn.

5
00:00:22.793 --> 00:00:24.900
They have the trucks and the people.

6
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.363
The jobs just don't come.

7
00:00:26.963 --> 00:00:30.793
And for a large customer, a single station is too small.

8
00:00:31.393 --> 00:00:34.323
Together, the stations cover all of Norway.

9
00:00:34.323 --> 00:00:36.163
No one else can offer that.

10
00:00:37.867 --> 00:00:43.177
Put simply, Assist Link connects those who have jobs with the stations that can do them.

11
00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:54.687
In Assist Connect, customers with their own dispatch centre, such as insurers, assistance companies or a bus company, create an agreement and offer it to the stations.

12
00:00:55.287 --> 00:01:01.107
The stations accept and join, and jobs are sent out to many stations at once.

13
00:01:01.707 --> 00:01:05.528
In Assist Work, Assist itself is the dispatch centre.

14
00:01:05.528 --> 00:01:08.557
One-off customers order one job at a time.

15
00:01:08.557 --> 00:01:10.360
And it's rarely recovery.

16
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:15.047
It's special transport of machinery, buses, boats and containers.

17
00:01:15.647 --> 00:01:20.348
Everything lands in Assist Dispatch, the app the stations already use.

18
00:01:20.348 --> 00:01:28.207
That's where the job is received, carried out and invoiced, and where stations share jobs with their friend stations.

19
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.670
Assist is not the carrier, and not the middleman who buys and sells jobs.

20
00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:39.439
We own the connection and the rules, and we charge both sides.

21
00:01:39.439 --> 00:01:42.330
But we are never a party to the job itself.

22
00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:47.910
The station invoices the customer directly, and keeps the customer relationship.

23
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.991
The construction industry orders transport through Swipload.

24
00:01:53.991 --> 00:02:01.457
From 1 January 2027, one of the largest rental companies in Norway will order all its transport there.

25
00:02:01.457 --> 00:02:04.970
And the drivers do not want to work in two apps.

26
00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:12.550
Step 1 is therefore a direct connection into the station's Dispatch, with status sent back to Swipload.

27
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.254
It doesn't bring new jobs yet.

28
00:02:15.254 --> 00:02:19.603
But we keep the jobs in Assist, and the connection is generic.

29
00:02:19.603 --> 00:02:22.970
Swipload is the first user, and more can follow.

30
00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.829
Step 2 is where the volume comes.

31
00:02:25.829 --> 00:02:36.510
Swipload becomes a dispatch centre in Connect, and sends jobs out to more stations, including stations that have never driven for the construction industry.

32
00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:42.025
Today, only 3 of our 60 stations drive for these customers.

33
00:02:42.025 --> 00:02:45.190
And 100% of those we surveyed want to.

34
00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:53.130
Today, Assist earns revenue from licences, onboarding packages, integrations and training.

35
00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:57.414
With Assist Link, new revenue comes from both sides.

36
00:02:57.414 --> 00:03:03.720
The station pays an integration fee per job, and customers pay a subscription to Connect.

37
00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.408
When Assist has brought in the customer, there's a brokerage fee.

38
00:03:08.408 --> 00:03:13.880
And new special transport companies buy a Dispatch licence, because they want the jobs.

39
00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:19.589
A 3,000 NOK job via Swipload earns Assist about 60 NOK.

40
00:03:19.589 --> 00:03:26.370
The same job from a direct customer earns 210 NOK, plus the subscription.

41
00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.329
Swipload brings volume and proof.

42
00:03:29.329 --> 00:03:31.760
Direct customers bring the margin.

43
00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:39.177
Together, Assist Link turns the station community into one nationwide provider.

44
00:03:39.777 --> 00:03:43.358
Customers get the whole country through a single platform.

45
00:03:43.358 --> 00:03:46.817
Stations get jobs when they would otherwise stand still.

46
00:03:47.417 --> 00:03:49.340
It starts with one connection.

47
00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.007
And we're building it now.
